WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Speaker 1: Students in Nashville, Tennessee, the&nbsp;
site of a recent horrifying mass school shooting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:11.940
walked out, rallied and marched yesterday for&nbsp;
stricter gun safety laws for any gun safety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.800
laws. And of course, we are yet again of mass&nbsp;
shootings that essentially no other country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:24.360
has. And then we immediately say, some of us say&nbsp;
we have to do something and Republicans block the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:29.520
idea of doing anything. And next thing you know,&nbsp;
we've moved on and it's the next mass shooting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:35.340
A couple of articles to look at. Chalkbeat&nbsp;
Tennessee reports. Nashville Students Rally for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:42.180
Tougher Gun Laws as Governor Seeks armed guards&nbsp;
for every school. Some say armed the teachers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.160
maybe armed the students. Right. I mean, how&nbsp;
far are we going to go? More than a thousand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:53.280
Nashville area students walked out of school on&nbsp;
Monday, converging outside the Tennessee state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.280 --> 00:01:00.060
capitol to demand stronger gun laws after last&nbsp;
week's mass shooting at a small private school in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:07.500
the city. This started at 10:13 a.m.. It was a&nbsp;
week since Nashville police received that first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:14.040
call about the shooter at the Covenant School.&nbsp;
Three children and three adult staff members were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:19.560
killed. We have a little more information about&nbsp;
the shooting, The Tennessean reports. Students&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:28.020
demand gun control. Shooter fired 152 rounds&nbsp;
in about a 14 minute incident. And, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:34.860
that has to have something to do with the&nbsp;
guns employed. You're not going to do that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:42.300
with a handgun. And so those who say this has&nbsp;
nothing to do with guns, by literal definition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:49.920
can't possibly be correct. Now, I think&nbsp;
it's important to contextualize all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:56.220
these events. I mean, think of it a week ago.&nbsp;
Shooting in Nashville. Six dead, three kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:03.600
three adults. Rallies, marches, demands for gun&nbsp;
safety. Republicans saying arming the teachers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:10.500
and put armed guards in school. But meanwhile,&nbsp;
in this week, how many mass shootings have there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:16.440
been? How many mass shootings have there been just&nbsp;
in the last week? Because yesterday there was one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:21.060
in Baltimore. And I'm looking at my list here.&nbsp;
And of course, it's very hard to keep up because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:28.740
there are so many. Yesterday, a mass shooting in&nbsp;
Baltimore and then also one in Mesa, Arizona. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:35.160
there was a mass shooting yesterday in Hampton,&nbsp;
Virginia. Another one on Sunday in Petersburg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:41.160
Virginia. The point is, just in the intervening&nbsp;
time between the Nashville shooting and today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.420
and we follow all of the lives affected,&nbsp;
Everything that's taken place, all of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.680
discourse and discourse may be a bit of a generous&nbsp;
term in some of these cases. We follow all of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.080
There have been so many mass shootings since,&nbsp;
most of which you and I haven't heard of,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:02.400
unless we went out looking for that information.&nbsp;
And so this really is an epidemic. We continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:12.660
to see one side that says don't do anything about&nbsp;
guns. And then we see our side say, listen, there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:19.440
are things we can try. And again, I outlined last&nbsp;
week my ten point plan for things that we could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:27.720
try. But there is an intransigent intransigence&nbsp;
and a recalcitrance to this discussion. And among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:34.320
half of those who could be part of the solution&nbsp;
here. And so it's a great thing what the students&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:40.320
in Nashville did. And I continue to hope that&nbsp;
we can do something. We can't give up, as I said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.900
last week, although it would be logical to think&nbsp;
maybe, maybe we should. What else can we do? We've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:52.380
tried everything to convince these people that&nbsp;
it's worth at least trying some gun safety. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.240
we really can't give up because otherwise people&nbsp;
will continue to die. So good for the students in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:01.985
Nashville, Tennessee. And of course, we will&nbsp;
follow whether any change does take place t

